            {
                "entry_id": "ec21b6d3-65b7-3643-8239-0f06637d27b7",
                "word": "cordate",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "5f7ed89c-dd78-4b8a-833b-86ba5bb592c6",
                        "entry_id": "ec21b6d3-65b7-3643-8239-0f06637d27b7",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "cordates"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "88e5d64c-0326-37b2-a731-9a8a6bdbbdb3",
                        "entry_id": "ec21b6d3-65b7-3643-8239-0f06637d27b7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Any animal with a heart."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "99eedcc1-8256-42f2-8c23-aab7541b70c9",
                                "sense_id": "88e5d64c-0326-37b2-a731-9a8a6bdbbdb3",
                                "text": "If, for instance, the context:"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d88b2bf4-72db-4887-919e-6bdb1b3f3467",
                                "sense_id": "88e5d64c-0326-37b2-a731-9a8a6bdbbdb3",
                                "text": "The organisms in any sample of tigers will almost always happen to exemplify genetic properties more specific than the property shared by exactly the tigers, as well as a number of more inclusive ones such as properties common to all mammals or to all cordates."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b24b019b-1aa0-41a0-9f64-13be55a4d10d",
                                "sense_id": "88e5d64c-0326-37b2-a731-9a8a6bdbbdb3",
                                "text": "Sciences of cordates — creatures with hearts — are, for example, less general or comprehensive than sciences of living things, and the latter are less comprehensive and general than sciences of moving things."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "971e0ad9-df71-45ce-8b71-86c47c38d612",
                                "sense_id": "88e5d64c-0326-37b2-a731-9a8a6bdbbdb3",
                                "text": "It is the coextension problem, the problem of the renates and the cordates, the creatures with kidneys and the creatures with hearts."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b1c2b097-9375-4827-846f-92711a22d2ba",
                                "sense_id": "88e5d64c-0326-37b2-a731-9a8a6bdbbdb3",
                                "text": "However, the property of being a cordate and the property of being a renate are different properties; the former has something to do with hearts and the latter has something to do with kidneys."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b2877513-e617-36f8-a620-df60ed672450",
                        "entry_id": "ec21b6d3-65b7-3643-8239-0f06637d27b7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A heart-shaped hand axe."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "dbcebe8b-d1f6-47ae-a8de-3e216298fc1e",
                                "sense_id": "b2877513-e617-36f8-a620-df60ed672450",
                                "text": "Slightly derived handaxes from the Mildenhall glaciofluvial sands, generally in fresh condition and dominated by ovates and cordates."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d92b0643-b59b-4819-a012-98d96793742b",
                                "sense_id": "b2877513-e617-36f8-a620-df60ed672450",
                                "text": "The upper loam (E) has been reported to have yielded several white-patinated implements, including a large number of pointed handaxes, cordates, ovates and cleavers."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9c919728-4109-4806-9558-ff3b4b0cf268",
                                "sense_id": "b2877513-e617-36f8-a620-df60ed672450",
                                "text": "Of the 58 ovates, cordates and cleavers examined, 21 have a tranchet sharpened edge, and 14 are twisted."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2f1a9d53-c77e-3c24-b67d-a136ac25fafc",
                        "entry_id": "ec21b6d3-65b7-3643-8239-0f06637d27b7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Misspelling of chordate."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "alt-of",
                            "misspelling"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0722d04b-d276-4756-af75-8dd16efab329",
                                "sense_id": "2f1a9d53-c77e-3c24-b67d-a136ac25fafc",
                                "text": "For quotations using this term, see Citations:cordate."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
